                        ],
                        "form": "more squamous"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "22d44668-a5a8-40b7-9752-29333f0891c1",
                        "entry_id": "78b6564f-ed37-337d-99de-a66a3868288f",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most squamous"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1c8dae6d-b07d-32e3-92e6-9263ca2b7847",
                        "entry_id": "78b6564f-ed37-337d-99de-a66a3868288f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Covered with, made of, or resembling scales; scaly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c4f04d2-7344-4867-ad27-ebb3824a6354",
                                "sense_id": "1c8dae6d-b07d-32e3-92e6-9263ca2b7847",
                                "text": "In the squamous heads of Scabius, Knapweed, and the elegant Jacea Pinea, and in the Scaly composure of the Oak-Rose, which some years most aboundeth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40177b68-7ad2-4ca4-8ff9-707c7c294359",
                                "sense_id": "1c8dae6d-b07d-32e3-92e6-9263ca2b7847",
                                "text": "I might call it gigantic - tentacled - proboscidian - octopus-eyed - semi-amorphous - plastic - partly squamous and partly rugose - ugh!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "506bd84e-8da3-4d3c-bc8b-afd2f1c947da",
                                "sense_id": "1c8dae6d-b07d-32e3-92e6-9263ca2b7847",
                                "text": "We spread the papers on the least squamous section of the floor and lay down; the smell was not so bad at ground level."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a216feb-b0ba-42e4-8d06-d55af95cfe2e",
                                "sense_id": "1c8dae6d-b07d-32e3-92e6-9263ca2b7847",
                                "text": "(And we'll never find out whether the last thought to pass through the mind of the captain of the Thresher was, \"It's squamous and rugose,\" or simply, \"It's squamous!\")"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ecef402d-89f1-3f42-ae6f-d28b54513cf5",
                        "entry_id": "78b6564f-ed37-337d-99de-a66a3868288f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to the squamosal bone; squamosal"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "90f0f585-077c-31e3-9d3c-e67c52716327",
                        "entry_id": "78b6564f-ed37-337d-99de-a66a3868288f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to an epithelium with cells that are wider than their height (flat and scale-like)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
